\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 2. HOW the Data Will Be Pulled Simultaneously\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 To prevent your bot from hitting exchange rate limits or bottlenecking your execution pipeline, the data is pulled using a decoupled, non-blocking network pattern:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Single-Session Async Multiplexing:
\f0\b0  Instead of opening and closing connections sequentially (Coin 1, then Coin 2, then Coin 3), the 10-minute thread opens a single asynchronous HTTP client session.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Parallel Batch Requests:
\f0\b0  The thread fires all 20 required network requests (1 Order Book request + 1 Candle Snapshot request per coin $\\times$ 10 coins) at the exact same millisecond.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The API Target:
\f0\b0  All requests hit Hyperliquid\'92s unified, public HTTP POST /info gateway endpoint. This gateway is designed for rapid high-volume reads and does not require private API key authentication, keeping your actual trading keys completely clear of read-rate traffic.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Concurrent Ingestion (Gathering):
\f0\b0  The bot waits for all 20 network responses to return concurrently\'97which takes roughly 200 to 400 milliseconds total.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Payload Structuring:
\f0\b0  As soon as the raw JSON packets hit the bot, the math engine structures them into 10 separate text blocks (one for each coin) containing the calculated indicators, price math, and order book delta.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 The Concurrent Selection Pipeline\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 1. The Parallel Prompt Fan-Out\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 The bot duplicates your exact mathematical scalping prompt into 10 distinct payloads (one for each token: PEPE, WIF, POPCAT, etc.), substituting the unique technical indicators and order book data for each coin. These 10 payloads are fired to your AI providers simultaneously using parallel API workers.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 2. Output Aggregation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Within seconds, the thread collects 10 structured JSON responses. The raw data state looks like this:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 WIF $\\rightarrow$ \{"direction": "wait", "confidence": 0.30\}\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 PEPE $\\rightarrow$ \{"direction": "long", "confidence": 0.88\}\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 POPCAT $\\rightarrow$ \{"direction": "short", "confidence": 0.94\}\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 SUI $\\rightarrow$ \{"direction": "wait", "confidence": 0.15\}\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}and so on\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
