\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 3. The Strict "WAIT" Filter\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 The code executes an instant filtration pass. Any asset that returns "direction": "wait" is completely thrown out of the candidate pool, regardless of how high its confidence value is (e.g., a high-confidence wait is still a pass). This isolates only active, high-velocity entry setups.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 4. Confidence Showdown & Winner Selection\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 The bot scans the remaining candidates (LONG or SHORT) and runs a max-value sort on the confidence key.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 $$\\text\{Winning Asset\} = \\max(\\text\{Confidence of Non-Wait Signals\})$$\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 Using the example above, POPCAT ($0.94$ Short) beats PEPE ($0.88$ Long). POPCAT is crowned the definitive winner of the 10-minute cycle.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 5. Redis State Handoff\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 The thread writes the winning token name to active_asset in Redis, updates the active signal direction to short, and flags it as is_fresh.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 How the Sniper Loop & System Interactivity Respond\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 Immediate Sniper Execution\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Because your trading_loop() runs on a ultra-fast 300ms cycle, it instantly catches the update in Redis. Since the confidence is high ($\\ge 0.80$), it bypasses the OBI gate, sets the leverage, and fires a market short order for POPCAT to the Hyperliquid L1 network, placing the tight $0.15\\%$ reduce-only TP/SL limit orders on the exchange.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 System Safety: The "All-Wait" Fallback\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 If the entire market is sideways and all 10 coins return a "direction": "wait", the system records a global WAIT status to Redis, logs it to Supabase, and opens no positions for that 10-minute cycle.\
Because you are scanning a wide basket of high-volatility assets simultaneously, the probability of hitting a 10-coin synchronized dead zone is low. This lets you completely delete the artificial "3-waits" forced override rule, protecting your trading capital from being pushed into non-trending markets.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

