\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 How the Voting System Works Now (Single-Asset Ensemble)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 Right now, your bot uses an 
\f1\b Ensemble Voting Engine
\f2\b0  for a single asset. When 
\f5\fs26 run_ai_signal()
\f2\fs24  fires, it sends the technical data payload to all configured providers in parallel. Because you use multiple distinct Gemini API keys, the system treats each key as an 
\f1\b individual, isolated AI agent
\f2\b0 .\
Each key gets an independent vote (
\f5\fs26 LONG
\f2\fs24 , 
\f5\fs26 SHORT
\f2\fs24 , or 
\f5\fs26 WAIT
\f2\fs24 ). The system tallies them up, and the direction with the maximum votes wins.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

